        <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Milestones and Recommended Actions - TCC:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><span data-field="milestone_1">{{ milestone_1 }}</span> Summer courses at TCC can help accelerate your time to transfer, and help you stay on track. Talk to your advisor about planning summer courses.</li>
            <li><span data-field="milestone_2">{{ milestone_2 }}</span> Consider a campus tour of Northeastern State University and connect with a NSU academic advisor, to ensure you are on track to transfer. Your TCC academic advisor can assist in planning these actions.</li>
            <li><span data-field="milestone_3">{{ milestone_3 }}</span> After semester three coursework, apply for admission at Northeastern State University as a transfer student (<a href="https://apply.nsuk.edu/">https://apply.nsuk.edu/</a>).</li>
            <li><span data-field="milestone_4">{{ milestone_4 }}</span> Congratulations you are about to earn your A.S. in Biotechnology. Be sure to apply for graduation at <a href="https://www.tulsa.edu/students/resources/graduation">https://www.tulsa.edu/students/resources/graduation</a>.</li>
            <li><span data-field="milestone_5">{{ milestone_5 }}</span> Submit an official TCC transcript to NSU (<a href="https://www.tulsa.edu/student-resources/student-records/requesting-and-submitting-transcripts">https://www.tulsa.edu/student-resources/student-records/requesting-and-submitting-transcripts</a>).</li>
            <li><span data-field="milestone_6">{{ milestone_6 }}</span> If you have not earned an Associate in Arts or an Associate in Science from TCC, and have completed 60 credit hours, with 15 of those hours completed at TCC, email <span data-field="email_address">{{ email_address }}</span> to see if you qualify for a degree through the Reverse Transfer program.</li>
        </ul>

